In plain CSS, wrap your declaration in a media query using the breakpoint's `--breakpoint-*` value (or use the `theme()` function), e.g.:

```css
.my-class {
  --my-var: 1rem;
}
@media (width >= theme(--breakpoint-md)) {
  .my-class { --my-var: 2rem; }
}
```

**Source:** `docs/responsive-design.mdx`, "Using custom breakpoints → Customizing your theme" — breakpoints are exposed as `--breakpoint-*` theme variables (e.g. `--breakpoint-md: 48rem`), and the corresponding utility variants compile to `@media (width >= 48rem) { ... }`. For raw CSS you target the same breakpoint by writing that media query directly (or referencing `theme(--breakpoint-md)`).

